Before each iteration, $live$ equals the probability that no
preceding entry has invalidated the artifact. The recurrence
can accept a different conditional probability at each event;
the estimates must then describe executions that actually
survived to that event. Offline, compare predicted first-miss
times with measured survival by workload phase rather than
pooling pre- and post-retirement counters. Sparse samples may
not support a useful estimate.
